---
import { Fragment } from 'astro/jsx-runtime';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import PhoneLink from '../components/PhoneLink.astro';
import PriceTable from '../components/PriceTable.astro';
import BreadcrumbSchema from '../components/Schema/Breadcrumb.astro';
import BreadcrumbNav from '../components/BreadcrumbNav.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { pricingTable, pricingPolicy } from '../data/pricing';
import { jobPhotos } from '../data/jobPhotos';

const doubleInstall = jobPhotos.find((p) => p.id === 'double-beige-raised')!;
const openerInstall = jobPhotos.find((p) => p.id === 'chamberlain-new-install')!;
const bottomBracket = jobPhotos.find((p) => p.id === 'wayne-dalton-bottom-bracket')!;

const title = `Garage Door Repair Pricing in Stittsville | Typical Ranges`;
const description = `Garage door repair pricing in Stittsville — published typical ranges. Springs $250–$350, cables $150–$250, openers $150–$300. Free on-site written quote. Call ${site.phone}.`;

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Pricing', path: '/pricing/' },
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <BreadcrumbSchema crumbs={crumbs} />
  </Fragment>

  <Hero
    title="Garage Door Repair Pricing in Stittsville"
    subtitle="Published starting rates — not a teaser quote that doubles when the van arrives on Hazeldean."
  />

  <div class="container-page border-b border-primary-100 bg-primary-50/50 py-3 md:py-4">
    <BreadcrumbNav crumbs={crumbs} />
  </div>

  <article class="container-page section-pad prose-content prose-wide max-w-none">
    <p>
      Stittsville homeowners asked for one page that answers “what will this actually cost?” without a sales call. This is that page — tied to our live price table, free on-site estimate policy, and the same typical ranges we use on site in Jackson Trails, Fairwinds, and Stittsville.
    </p>

    <h2>Free on-site estimate — how quoting works</h2>
    <p>
      Every visit includes diagnosis, a walkthrough of what failed, and a <strong>written quote before any repair begins</strong>. There is no separate dispatch or service-call fee — you approve the price on site, then we fix it. That is the same transparent model homeowners expect from reputable Ottawa garage door shops.
    </p>
    <p>
      We avoid the $69 bait-and-switch you see in ads — low dispatch quotes that balloon once someone is in your garage. The ranges below are what Stittsville homeowners typically pay for parts, labour, and a safety check. Seniors and veterans receive <strong>{pricingPolicy.seniorsVeteransDiscountPercent}% off repairs</strong>.
    </p>

    <h2>Typical price ranges for common jobs</h2>
    <p>
      The table below lists typical ranges for the repairs we do most often in Stittsville. Final cost depends on door size (single vs double vs three-car), parts quality, and what we find once the door is inspected — but these numbers are honest anchors, not footnotes in fine print.
    </p>
    <div class="not-prose my-8">
      <PriceTable rows={pricingTable} />
    </div>
    <p>
      Want deeper context on what drives price up or down? Read our <a href="/resources/stittsville-pricing-guide/">Stittsville garage door pricing guide (2026)</a>.
    </p>

    <aside class="not-prose mx-auto my-10 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="grid overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-primary-100 bg-white shadow-sm md:grid-cols-[440px,1fr]">
        <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden bg-primary-50 md:aspect-auto md:h-full">
          <img
            src={doubleInstall.src}
            alt={doubleInstall.alt}
            width={doubleInstall.width}
            height={doubleInstall.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col justify-center p-5 md:p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-600">Featured install</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg text-primary-900">Pair of new doors — full driveway swap</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-primary-700">
            Two-door jobs price differently than one. Door pricing scales close to linearly, but
            springs, openers, and labour see a small discount when both bays are done in a single
            visit. We quote each combination separately on site, in writing, before any work begins.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <h2>Why prices vary between homes</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Door size and weight.</strong> A heavy wood-look carriage door on Crossing Bridge Way needs different springs and rollers than a standard steel double-car in Jackson Trails. More weight means higher-rated springs, more labour to balance, and sometimes upgraded hardware.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Opener brand and age.</strong> LiftMaster and Chamberlain belt-drive units from the late 2000s share common wear parts we stock. Older Genie screw-drive models or discontinued boards may need more time to source — we tell you before we order.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Parts quality.</strong> We can match OEM-grade springs and rollers or explain when a budget part is appropriate on an older door you plan to replace within a year. You choose after you see the quote — not after the work is half done.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What else failed at the same time.</strong> A spring snap often stresses cables and drums. A bent track may have damaged rollers and hinges. We list everything on the written quote so you are not surprised by “while we were here” add-ons.
    </p>

    <h2>What drives the price up</h2>
    <ul class="mb-8 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Three-car doors and custom carriage panels in Crossing Bridge Estates</li>
      <li>High-cycle or oversized torsion springs on oversized double doors</li>
      <li>Jackshaft or wall-mount opener installs where ceiling clearance is tight</li>
      <li>Multiple failed components (spring + cable + drum) from continuing to run a crooked door</li>
      <li>After-hours emergency dispatch between 10 PM and 7 AM — surcharge quoted before we roll out</li>
    </ul>

    <aside class="not-prose mx-auto my-10 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="grid overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-primary-100 bg-white shadow-sm md:grid-cols-[440px,1fr]">
        <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden bg-primary-50 md:aspect-auto md:h-full">
          <img
            src={bottomBracket.src}
            alt={bottomBracket.alt}
            width={bottomBracket.width}
            height={bottomBracket.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col justify-center p-5 md:p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-600">Cable repair detail</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg text-primary-900">Wayne Dalton retainer — full bottom-end rebuild</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-primary-700">
            Wayne Dalton doors use a proprietary bottom retainer for the seal — it must be removed
            and reset correctly any time the cable or roller is replaced. On this Stittsville job we
            fitted a new bottom weather seal, lift cable, nylon roller, and bottom bracket in one
            visit. The retainer hardware and seal alignment time pushes this job to the higher end of
            cable-repair pricing.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <h2>What drives the price down</h2>
    <ul class="mb-8 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>Single-component fixes (sensor alignment, limit adjustment, one roller set)</li>
      <li>Standard-size doors with parts on the truck — common in Fairwinds and Wyldewood steel setups</li>
      <li>Single-component fixes completed in one visit without extra trip charges</li>
      <li>Annual <a href="/services/maintenance/">maintenance tune-ups</a> that prevent opener and cable failures later</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Phone quotes vs on-site quotes</h2>
    <p>
      We can give ranges for common jobs if you describe door size and symptoms — a loud bang usually means <a href="/services/spring-repair/">spring repair ($250–$350)</a>; a humming motor with no movement often means <a href="/services/opener-repair/">opener repair ($150–$300)</a>. We confirm the final number in writing on site before work starts.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>We will not quote you a final price over the phone for a complex repair, because we would be guessing.</strong> We can share the typical range from the table below, then confirm the exact number in writing on site after we inspect the door — free estimate, no dispatch fee.
    </p>

    <h2>Compare jobs side by side</h2>
    <p>
      Homeowners often ask whether to repair or replace. If a Fairwinds door from 1998 has a failed spring but sound panels and tracks, <a href="/services/spring-repair/">spring repair</a> plus a <a href="/services/maintenance/">tune-up</a> is usually the right economics. If Amberwood steel is rusted through the bottom section and the springs are original, <a href="/services/new-door-installation/">new door installation</a> may cost less over five years than repeated panel patches. We walk through that math on site — with real numbers from the table above, not a sales script.
    </p>
    <p>
      Opener repair ($150–$300) makes sense when the rail, motor, and door are sound. New opener installation ($650–$950 installed) makes sense when the unit is obsolete, loud, or missing modern safety features. Panel repair ($150–$400 in place) makes sense when the steel is still sound; we will say so if a full door swap is smarter.
    </p>

    <aside class="not-prose mx-auto my-10 max-w-4xl">
      <div class="grid overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-primary-100 bg-white shadow-sm md:grid-cols-[440px,1fr]">
        <div class="aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden bg-primary-50 md:aspect-auto md:h-full">
          <img
            src={openerInstall.src}
            alt={openerInstall.alt}
            width={openerInstall.width}
            height={openerInstall.height}
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col justify-center p-5 md:p-6">
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-600">Opener install</p>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg text-primary-900">New Chamberlain chain-drive opener</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-primary-700">
            Chain-drive units are the budget-friendly workhorse — durable and well-suited to detached
            garages or homes where opener noise is not a concern. For Stittsville garages that share
            a wall with a bedroom (common in Jackson Trails splits) we recommend stepping up to a
            belt-drive instead. Installed pricing covers the unit, rail, safety sensors, wall
            console, remotes, and a full safety and auto-reverse test before we hand over the
            remotes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <h2>Warranty and payment</h2>
    <p>
      Parts we supply carry a one-year warranty against defect; labour is covered for the same period on standard repairs. Payment is due on completion by e-transfer, card, or cheque — we leave a written invoice for your records and insurance if a panel was hit by a vehicle backing out toward Main Street.
    </p>
    <p>
      Tax is applied as required on parts and labour. If a job needs a special-order door, we quote lead time before you commit — no deposit surprises for Crossing Bridge carriage profiles or discontinued colours. Panel work is in-place repair only; we do not order replacement sections.
    </p>

    <h2>Get an exact quote in 60 seconds</h2>
    <p>
      Call {site.phone}, describe what the door is doing, and give your street — Jackson Trails, Amberwood, Bryanston Gate, or anywhere in Stittsville. We will slot a same-day window when possible and walk you through the written quote on arrival. Most homeowners know yes or no within a minute of reading it.
    </p>
    <p>
      For non-urgent work you can also use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> with your address and symptoms — we will call back with a typical range before anyone drives out past the Johnny Leroux Community Arena or west toward Saunders Farm.
    </p>

    <div class="card mt-12 bg-primary-50 text-center not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl">Ready for a written quote on site?</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-primary-700">No surprise invoices — Stittsville pricing you can plan around.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <PhoneLink showIcon />
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn-secondary">Send a message</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
